# Line endings are normative in this repo, not a checkout detail.
#
# deploy/deploy.ps1 scp's deploy/remote-deploy.sh straight from the WORKING COPY,
# so on a machine with core.autocrlf=true a CRLF checkout hands bash a shebang
# ending in \r. That is unrunnable, and it is exactly how iFilter's
# public/scripts/amos.sh and the iShield installer's deploy broke. The rule lives
# here rather than in anyone's git config because no other checkout inherits a
# git config.
#
# remote-deploy.sh also refuses a tree with CRLF in .sh/.js/.json/.conf, so a
# regression here fails the deploy rather than reaching the server.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
